          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="google-obj" edge="1" parent="1" source="google-gw" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;arcSize=16;strokeColor=#2ee6c5;strokeWidth=1.6;startArrow=oval;startFill=1;startSize=6;endArrow=block;endFill=1;endSize=7;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#e6e8f0;labelBackgroundColor=#161823;exitX=0;exitY=0.75;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="store" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="1020" y="712" />
              <mxPoint x="1020" y="498" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cap0" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#e6e8f0;fillColor=#1d2030;strokeColor=#3a3f55;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The runner and every cluster call the ingress origin, server.public_url: /api/v1 for the scenarios, /worker/v1 and /state/v1 for workers. Signed object URLs are user delegation SAS URLs that Pods fetch from Blob Storage directly." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="100" width="383" x="30" y="860" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cap1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#e6e8f0;fillColor=#1d2030;strokeColor=#3a3f55;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Trust anchors and egress&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Everyone trusts system roots: the managed ingress certificate and the Blob Storage endpoint. Each cluster egresses through its own NAT. The app managed identity signs in to PostgreSQL, Blob Storage and Key Vault through Entra ID." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="100" width="383" x="429" y="860" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cap2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#e6e8f0;fillColor=#1d2030;strokeColor=#3a3f55;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b&gt;For&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ingress, TLS and its certificate come with Container Apps, so there is no load balancer or gateway to run. Entra database authentication, Key Vault keys and user delegation SAS exercise the Azure drivers." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="100" width="383" x="828" y="860" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cap3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=12;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#e6e8f0;fillColor=#1d2030;strokeColor=#3a3f55;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Against&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Private access to the database needs a VNet-integrated environment. A custom domain needs DNS validation. Replicas must stay fixed at two for the scheduler. Remote server coverage needs its own collection." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="100" width="383" x="1227" y="860" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
